{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-77622-r4523281","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Katchi Biryani","sourcePageId":77622,"sourceRevision":"4523281","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T17:24:39Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Katchi%20Biryani&oldid=4523281","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:10.350Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Indian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for biryani","Category:Recipes using black cardamom","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using food coloring","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"819523b86892e07a6661d56bfd2ceef27b4242169819f7861277c06ca6fd1de1","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Cuisine of India]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Marinade ===\n* 4 large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]s, finely [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] and fried in ghee or butter\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yoghurt]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Chiles|green chiles]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1 bunch [[Cookbook:Mint|mint leaves]], chopped\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]] or [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]], to taste\n* 1 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Ginger Garlic Paste|ginger-garlic paste]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Pound|lbs]] [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]]\n\n=== Rice ===\n* Black [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]] pods\n* Black [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds (kala zeera)\n* Whole black [[Cookbook:Peppercorn|peppercorns]]\n* Salt, to taste\n* 1 Tbsp oil\n* 2 ¾ cups uncooked [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n\n=== Assembly ===\n* 8 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], in 4 pieces\n* [[Cookbook:Lemon|Lemon]] juice\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] of [[Cookbook:Saffron|saffron]] or a few drops yellow food coloring\n* [[Cookbook:Milk|Milk]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Chili Pepper|green chillies]], whole\n* 1 bunch [[Cookbook:Cilantro|coriander leaves]], chopped\n* Fried [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n* [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|Garam masala]] powder\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Combine fried onions, yoghurt, chopped green peppers, chopped mint leaves, ghee, garam masala powder, salt, ginger garlic paste. Add the chicken pieces, and leave this to [[Cookbook:Marinating|marinate]] at least 4–5 hours.\n# Bring a pot of water to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Add cardamom, black cumin, peppercorns, cinnamon stick, salt, and oil. When the water boils, mix in the rice.\n# Cook the rice until tender but not completely cooked—it will cook more later. Drain the water from the rice.\n# Add a very thin layer of rice on the bottom of the pot to prevent the meat from sticking. Add the marinated chicken on top. Top the chicken with the remaining drained rice.\n# Combine the saffron and milk. Place one butter chunk in each quadrant of the pot. Pour the lemon juice and saffron milk over the rice, then stick the whole chiles in the rice.\n# Add the chopped coriander leaves, fried onions, and a sprinkle of garam masala.\n# Cover pot completely with [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]] so no steam can escape. Cook over high heat for about 10 minutes.\n# Reduce heat to medium. Continue cooking about 30–35 minutes, rotating the pot every 10 minutes for even heating.\n# Check to make sure the meat and rice are fully cooked.\n# Serve.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* You can substitute [[Cookbook:Lamb|lamb]] or [[Cookbook:Goat|goat]] for the chicken—in this case, marinate for 12 hours.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for biryani]]\n[[Category:Recipes using black cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using food coloring]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Katchi Biryani","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 large onions, finely sliced and fried in ghee or butter","sourceText":"4 large onions, finely sliced and fried in ghee or butter","amountText":"4 large onions, finely sliced and fried in ghee or butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cups yoghurt","sourceText":"2 cups yoghurt","amountText":"2 cups yoghurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 green chiles, chopped","sourceText":"3 green chiles, chopped","amountText":"3 green chiles, chopped","amoun